# Merged: rask (base) + lance-ns main@083b49a. lance-ns's whole file was the single line `.git`,
# which rask's `.git/` already covers for a normal repo — the bare form is kept because a git
# WORKTREE has `.git` as a FILE, and `.git/` (directory-anchored) would not match it.
#
# CAREFUL: .helmignore also removes files from `.Files`, not just from the packaged tarball.
# chart/templates/alerting.yaml does `.Files.Get "alerting/rules.yml"`, so nothing here may match
# `alerting/**` — an over-broad pattern would render an EMPTY alert-rules ConfigMap silently.
.git/
.git
*.md
.DS_Store
*.tmp
ci/
# Merge-conflict leftovers: a stray values.yaml.orig would otherwise ship inside the chart.
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak

# THE CNPG CRDs, 1.19 MB in one file — deliberately NOT packaged.
#
# Helm stores the whole chart in the release Secret, which Kubernetes caps at 1 MiB. Measured
# 2026-08-18: revision 34 decoded to 1,046,844 bytes against a 1,048,576 limit — 1.7 KB of headroom —
# and the next chart edit made every `helm upgrade` fail with "Secret ... is invalid: data: Too long".
# The estate was one comment away from being undeployable, and had been for days.
#
# Moving them out costs nothing that Helm was providing: a `crds/` directory is installed ONCE and
# never upgraded or deleted by Helm, so it was already not managing their lifecycle. `make k3s-crds`
# applies them server-side, and `k3s-up` depends on it — which also fixes the upgrade case the
# `crds/` dir silently did not cover.
#
# They stay vendored (not left to the subchart) for the reason values.yaml gives: CNPG ships its CRDs
# as TEMPLATES, so on a cold install Helm cannot map our `Cluster` CR in the same release. That is why
# `cloudnative-pg.crds.create` is false, and it still is.
crds-bootstrap/
